---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StructureNext from "../../components/StructureNext.astro";
import LessonIllustration from "../../components/LessonIllustration.astro";
import StructureKindTag from "../../components/StructureKindTag.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Registers"
  description="Compare ways to choose or preserve answers in one shared field."
  territory="Structures"
  sheetTitle="Registers"
>
  <article class="register-family">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="territory-label">Structure family</p>
      <h1>Registers</h1>
      <p>
        The beacon list is settled, but the ranger still needs one answer:
        is the Eagle Creek trail open? Alice, Bob, and Carol discover that one
        shared field still needs a rule when reports arrive at the same time.
      </p>
      <LessonIllustration id="structures-registers" />
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="lww-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <StructureKindTag kind="CRDT" />
          <h2 id="lww-title">LWWRegister</h2>
          <p>Use the time and author to choose one answer.</p>
        </div>
        <code>lww_register_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice reports <code>Trail open</code> while Bob reports
            <code>Trail closed</code>. A last-writer-wins register keeps one
            value. The hikers keep the value with the later time. If the
            times match, they compare the authors' names.
          </p>
          <p>
            Carol can receive the reports in either order and still choose the
            same value. The losing report is discarded, so readers do not see
            the disagreement.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Small settings that need one predictable answer</li>
            <li>Values where people trust timestamps to select one answer</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Text with a time and author</dd></div>
          <div><dt>How copies combine</dt><dd>Later time, then author</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What it remembers</dt><dd>The answer, time, and author</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/lww-register/">
        Open the LWWRegister lesson
      </a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="mv-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <StructureKindTag kind="CRDT" />
          <h2 id="mv-title">MvRegister</h2>
          <p>Keep competing answers until someone resolves them.</p>
        </div>
        <code>mv_register_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            The ranger cannot safely discard either trail report. The
            multi-value register keeps both Alice's and Bob's answers. Carol
            sees the disagreement instead of a silent winner.
          </p>
          <p>
            After Carol inspects the bridge, her next report can replace the
            answers she saw. A report she has not seen still remains.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Reviews where a person must resolve competing answers</li>
            <li>Values where losing a valid report would be harmful</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Answers with information about earlier answers</dd></div>
          <div><dt>How copies combine</dt><dd>Keep answers made at the same time</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What it remembers</dt><dd>Each remaining answer and its history</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/multi-value-register/">
        Open the MvRegister lesson
      </a>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="collection-title">
      <header>
        <div>
          <StructureKindTag kind="DDS" />
          <h2 id="collection-title">RegisterCollection</h2>
          <p>Keep numbered versions and choose how to read them.</p>
        </div>
        <code>register_collection_kernel</code>
      </header>
      <div class="structure-body">
        <div>
          <p>
            Alice and Bob submit reports before either sees the other. The
            ranger's service numbers and stores both versions. One reading
            method keeps the first answer that had no competition. Another
            returns the newest numbered answer.
          </p>
          <p>
            The collection does not compare clocks or combine the answers. It
            keeps the numbered versions so the reader can choose between the
            two rules.
          </p>
          <h3>Best for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Named fields that need a first or newest answer</li>
            <li>Shared work where old numbered versions still matter</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Updates</dt><dd>Answers numbered by one service</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Read rules</dt><dd>First uncontested or newest</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What it remembers</dt><dd>Answers and their numbers</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <a class="structure-link" href="/structures/register-collection/">
        Open the RegisterCollection lesson
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="family-comparison" aria-labelledby="register-choice-title">
      <h2 id="register-choice-title">Choose what disagreement means</h2>
      <table aria-label="Register comparison">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Need</th><th scope="col">Choose</th><th scope="col">Trade-off</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Use time to select one answer</th><td>LWWRegister</td><td>Discard the other answer</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Keep competing answers</th><td>MvRegister</td><td>Someone must resolve them later</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Choose from numbered answers</th><td>RegisterCollection</td><td>One service must order them</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <StructureNext />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .register-family {
    max-width: var(--measure-reading);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .page-intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  .page-intro > p:last-of-type {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .register-family > section:not(.family-comparison) {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    background: var(--clear);
  }

  section > header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  section h2,
  section header p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-block: var(--space-1);
  }

  section header code {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .structure-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(15rem, 0.7fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .structure-body :is(p, h3) {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .structure-body h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 0;
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
  }

  dl div {
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
  }

  dl div + div {
    border-top: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line-faint);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 700 0.8rem/1.3 var(--font-ui);
  }

  dd {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
  }

  .structure-link {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .family-comparison {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }

  :is(th, td) {
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-block: var(--rule-width) solid var(--line);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  th {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
  }

  @media (width < 48rem) {
    section > header,
    .structure-body {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    section > header {
      display: grid;
    }
  }
</style>
